          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Several Microsoft partner consultancies and boutique AI automation agencies in Sydney specialise in **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **AI agent architecture**, and **practical workflow automation** tailored for mid-market organisations. \n\n### 1. Premier Microsoft AI & Cloud Specialists\nThese consultancies bring deep technical capabilities across both low-code (Copilot Studio, Power Platform) and pro-code (Azure OpenAI, Azure AI Foundry, Semantic Kernel) ecosystems.\n\n* **Arinco** *(Sydney CBD - 24 Campbell St)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Cloud, Data, and AI engineering. They offer dedicated offerings like the **Copilot Studio Agent Builder Accelerator** and hands-on **Agentathons**.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Ideal for businesses that want to move beyond generic chat to build autonomous, multi-step agents that interact with enterprise databases and line-of-business software via APIs. They bridge low-code Copilot Studio tools with robust Azure AI governance.\n* **Engage Squared** *(Sydney & Melbourne)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Recognized as a Microsoft Copilot Specialisation partner. They focus on Copilot Studio agent builds, workflow automation, and organizational adoption.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Strong choice if user adoption, governance, and change management are top priorities. Their **Secure Agentic Foundations** accelerator helps mid-market IT leaders manage data oversharing (via Microsoft Purview/Entra ID) before deploying custom agents.\n* **Barhead Solutions** *(Sydney CBD - 123 Pitt St)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate, Dataverse) and Dynamics 365.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** If your mid-market automation relies heavily on CRM/ERP data (e.g., Dynamics 365, Salesforce, Dataverse), Barhead excels at embedding Copilot Studio agents directly into transactional workflows and automated approval loops.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Pragmatic, Mid-Market-First Consultancies\nThese firms operate without the overhead of enterprise tier-1 consultancies, delivering agile, fixed-scope, or outcome-focused automation.\n\n* **Frontrow Technology** *(Sydney)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Microsoft Copilot readiness, deployment, and custom Copilot Studio agent builds specifically for Sydney mid-market and lower enterprise clients.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Highly practical approach. They run fixed-scope assessments to remediate identity and SharePoint permission risks first, then build purpose-driven Copilot Studio agents grounded in company-specific operational data.\n* **Eagle360 Consulting** *(Sydney)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Microsoft Power Platform and Dynamics 365 Business Central automation.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Specifically tailored to Australian mid-market operational workflows. They specialize in building Copilot Studio agents that read/write into ERPs, process supplier invoices via AI Builder, and automate quote-to-cash sequences using Power Automate.\n* **IOTAI** *(North Sydney - 99 Walker St)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Custom Copilot Studio agents and workflow automation for SMBs and mid-market businesses.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Offers fast, fixed-fee deployment models (typically live in 2–4 weeks). They specialise in connecting Copilot agents not just to Microsoft 365, but also common Australian accounting and operations platforms like Xero and MYOB via custom connectors.\n* **Synenza** *(Sydney)*\n  * **Core Focus:** Copilot Studio agents, Power Platform integration, and Azure AI Foundry solutions.\n  * **Mid-Market Fit:** Focused on turning repetitive manual tasks (IT triage, HR policy discovery, invoice reconciliation) into automated agent flows using Power Automate and Dataverse.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Selecting a Consultant\n\n1. **How do they handle data security and \"oversharing\"?**\n   * *Why it matters:* Copilot and Copilot Studio respect existing SharePoint/OneDrive permissions. If your internal access controls are loose, deploying an agent can accidentally expose confidential executive or payroll data to general staff. A good partner will audit permissions and configure Microsoft Purview before deployment.\n2. **Low-Code vs. Pro-Code Integration:**\n   * If your workflows only involve SharePoint, Teams, and standard Microsoft 365 apps, standard **Copilot Studio + Power Automate** is sufficient.\n   * If you need the agent to query legacy SQL databases, proprietary APIs, or perform complex logic, ensure the consultant has engineering skills in **Azure AI Foundry, REST APIs, and Semantic Kernel**.\n3. **Licensing and Capacity Planning:**\n   * Microsoft Copilot Studio requires message/capacity credits, which are separate from standard Microsoft 365 Copilot user seats. A good consultant will help you model query volumes and licensing costs before building.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
